While npm installs in background, write source files. Start with shared layer + app skeleton.

Let me design the file tree:

```
src/
  main.tsx
  App.tsx
  vite-env.d.ts
  styles/global.css
  shared/
    copy/en.ts          -- all user-facing strings
    lib/money.ts        -- cents utils
    lib/money.test.ts
    lib/mealSlot.ts     -- cutoff logic (Asia/Shanghai)
    lib/mealSlot.test.ts
    lib/constants.ts    -- allergen catalog, spice levels, meal periods
    ui/theme.ts         -- AntD ConfigProvider theme
    ui/AppProviders.tsx
    ui/PriceText.tsx
    ui/DishImage.tsx
    ui/StateViews.tsx   -- LoadingView, EmptyView, ErrorView (actionable)
    ui/AppShell.tsx     -- responsive layout with nav (desktop sider/header, mobile drawer)
    api/types.ts        -- API DTO types
    api/http.ts         -- request client, ApiError, error mapping
    api/index.ts        -- endpoint functions
  features/
    auth/
      api.ts (or use shared/api)  -- keep endpoint functions in shared/api? Better: feature-local hooks. I'll do: shared/api/http.ts generic client; features/*/api.ts typed calls.
      AuthContext.tsx
      LoginPage.tsx
      RegisterPage.tsx
      guards.tsx (RequireAuth, RequireRole)
    menu/
      api.ts, hooks.ts
      MenuPage.tsx
      DishCard.tsx
      DishDetailModal.tsx
    cart/
      CartContext.tsx (reducer)
      cartReducer.ts + cartReducer.test.ts
      CartDrawer.tsx
      CheckoutPage.tsx
    orders/
      api.ts, hooks.ts
      OrdersPage.tsx
      OrderDetailPage.tsx (or modal)
    settings/
      api.ts, PreferencesPage.tsx, AddressesSection
    console/
      api.ts
      ConsoleLayout? (just pages)
      DishesAdminPage.tsx
      DishEditDrawer.tsx
      DailyMenuAdminPage.tsx
  router.tsx
```

Key design decisions:

Money: `formatCents(cents: number): string` -> `¥22.50`. All prices number (integer cents).

Meal slot logic (shared/lib/mealSlot.ts):
```ts
export type MealPeriod = 'LUNCH' | 'DINNER';
export const LUNCH_CUTOFF_HOUR = 10;
export const DINNER_CUTOFF_HOUR = 15;
export function resolveOrderableSlot(now: Date): { date: string; mealPeriod: MealPeriod }
```
Using Asia/Shanghai time. Get Shanghai time via Intl. If now < 10:00 -> today LUNCH; else if now < 15:00 -> today DINNER; else tomorrow LUNCH. But also lunch cutoff passed → today's dinner if not cutoff. Per PRD: "若默认餐次已截止，自动选择最近可订餐次：当日晚餐未截止则选当日晚餐，否则选次日午餐。" And default meal is lunch presumably. resolveOrderableSlot: if before 10:00 → today LUNCH; else if before 15:00 → today DINNER; else tomorrow LUNCH.

Also `isSlotOrderable(date, period, now)` for checkout validation display.

Date format YYYY-MM-DD via dayjs? In lib, use Intl to avoid dayjs dependency in lib... dayjs is fine (it's a dependency). Use dayjs with utc/timezone plugin? That requires dayjs/plugin/timezone which uses Intl — fine. Simpler: use Intl.DateTimeFormat with timeZone 'Asia/Shanghai' to get parts. I'll write a small helper using Intl.

For tests, resolveOrderableSlot(now) takes a Date so tests can inject.

HTTP client (shared/api/http.ts):
```ts
const API_BASE = import.meta.env.VITE_API_BASE_URL ?? '/api';
export class ApiError extends Error { status; code?; details? }
async function request<T>(path, {method, body, headers, idempotencyKey}): Promise<T>
```
- credentials: 'include' always
- JSON body
- 401 -> throw ApiError(401, 'UNAUTHORIZED')
- parse error body {code, message, details?} fallback to status text
- network failure (fetch throws) -> ApiError(0, 'NETWORK', actionable message)

Error mapping: mapApiError(err) -> user-friendly English message via copy file.

Auth flow: GET /auth/me on load; 401 -> not authenticated. Login mutation sets query data.

Cart: React context with reducer. CartItem: {key, dish (snapshot subset: id, name, priceCents, imageUrl), selectedOptions: [{groupId, groupName, itemId, itemName, extraPriceCents}], quantity, unitPriceCents}. key = dishId + sorted optionItemIds hash. Reducer actions: add (merge if same key, enforce cap 5 total), setQuantity, remove, clear. Persist to localStorage? Cart is frontend-held; localStorage persistence is allowed (only tokens forbidden). I'll persist cart in localStorage for UX. It's fine.

Allergen confirm: before adding to cart, check dish.allergens ∩ preferences.allergens; if hit, Modal.confirm (English) listing allergens, "Add anyway".

Checkout:
- query GET /ordering/slot suggestion (backend). If endpoint missing/error, fall back to client resolveOrderableSlot but display.
- DatePicker (today/tomorrow limited? allow up to +7 days but disable past and disable slots past cutoff for today). Simpler: Radio for date: suggested date options today/tomorrow; meal period radio Lunch/Dinner with cutoff disabling. Keep DatePicker per requirements: "使用 Ant Design 的 ... DatePicker". Use DatePicker with disabledDate (before today, after +7d) and meal period Select with disabled based on cutoff when date is today.
- Address: Radio list of saved addresses + "New address" with TextArea (max 200).
- Budget notice: if total > preferences.budgetCents -> Alert warning, not blocking.
- Idempotency-Key: useRef(uuid) generated when entering checkout / when cart changes; passed header. Disable submit while pending. On success: show success result with order number, date, period, address; clear cart.
- Error handling: ApiError code INSUFFICIENT_STOCK with details.items -> Alert listing dish names; DUPLICATE_ACTIVE_ORDER -> prompt with link to orders.

Orders: list (Table on desktop, List on mobile — use AntD List with cards for responsiveness simplicity), detail via Drawer/Modal, cancel button for PENDING with Popconfirm, invalidate queries.

Settings: Form with allergen Checkboxes, cuisine/category multi-select (from categories endpoint), spice Select, taste Select, budget InputNumber (yuan, convert to cents), recommended toggle Switch. Save via PUT.

Console:
- DishesAdminPage: Table (responsive scroll), Search input (max 50), category Select filter, "New Dish" button -> Drawer with Form: name, description, price (yuan InputNumber -> cents), categories (Select multiple, free? use Select mode="multiple" with options from categories endpoint + allow new via mode="tags"), protein Select, spice Select, allergens Checkbox group, listed Switch, image Upload (POST multipart, show preview), option groups editor (Form.List dynamic: group name, required switch, items with name + extra price).
- List/unlist: Switch in table with confirm.
- DailyMenuAdminPage: DatePicker (default tomorrow), table of menu entries for date with availableQuantity InputNumber, add dish (Select from listed dishes), remove, save (PUT).

API endpoints (typed calls per feature). Also need GET /menu/categories. And admin dishes list.

Copy file: centralize strings. To be pragmatic, I'll centralize in shared/copy/en.ts with sections and import as `t`. That's a lot of strings; I'll be reasonably thorough.

AppShell: AntD Layout; desktop: Sider or top header menu; mobile (Grid.useBreakpoint xs): header with menu button opening Drawer nav. Nav items depend on role: Menu, My Orders, Cart (badge), Settings, Console (admin only), Logout.

Route structure:
- /login, /register (redirect to / if authed)
- RequireAuth: / -> Navigate to /menu; /menu; /checkout; /orders; /orders/:id; /settings
- RequireRole ADMIN: /console/dishes, /console/daily-menu
- 403 Forbidden page, 404 NotFound.

Now write all files. This is a lot of writing — let me be efficient and write them in batches. I'll write thoughtfully to compile cleanly with strict TS (noUnusedLocals!).

Careful points:
- antd v5: use `App` component for message/modal context (App.useApp()). Use that instead of static message.
- TanStack Query v5 API: useMutation({mutationFn, onSuccess}), isPending.
- React Router v6: createBrowserRouter/RouterProvider or <Routes>. Use <Routes> with BrowserRouter in main.

Let me write shared layer first.

